


// transientDemand.js
//
// Real Nexus transient-demand calendar (2023-01-01 .. 2025-12-31), embedded
// directly from Nexus_Transient_Demand_v2.csv — the same file the Python
// training pipeline (rfp_xgboost_pipeline_v7_1.py, STAGE 2 "TRANSIENT JOIN")
// uses to build the tr_* features baked into rfp_training_data_complete_v3.csv.
//
// Columns per row (array-of-arrays to keep this file small):
//   [ date, totalOccPct, transientOccOfAvailable, transientRoomsTurnedAway,
//     displacementPressureCode, totalDisplacementCost, displacementCostPerRoom,
//     transientRevenue, transientADR, groupRoomsOnBooks ]
//
// displacementPressureCode uses the EXACT mapping from the pipeline's
// TR_CAT_MAPS["tr_displacement_pressure"]:  Low:0, Medium:1, High:2, Sold Out:3
//
// ── What this module reproduces EXACTLY vs. APPROXIMATES ───────────────────
//
// EXACT (byte-for-byte same method as the training pipeline's join_transient()):
//   tr_transient_occ_of_available   — mean of Transient_Occ_Of_Available over
//                                      [arrival, departure) stay window
//   tr_transient_rooms_turned_away  — mean of Transient_Rooms_Turned_Away over
//                                      the same window
//   tr_displacement_pressure        — modal (most frequent) daily category
//                                      over the window, mapped via TR_CAT_MAPS
//
// APPROXIMATED (the v3 training data already had these baked in by an earlier,
// undocumented feature-engineering stage — rfp_model_report_v7_1.docx Section
// 4.3 only describes the *shape* of the formulas, not the exact source series
// or window boundaries, so these are principled reconstructions from the real
// daily calendar using that documented shape, not a verified reproduction):
//   transient_displacement_cost   — mean(Displacement_Cost_Per_Room over stay
//                                    window) × room_block
//   occupancy_velocity_7_30d      — mean_7d(Total_Occupancy_Pct) − mean_30d(...)
//                                    as of inquiry_date (report 4.3: "velocity
//                                    = difference of short and long rolling means")
//   occupancy_acceleration        — velocity_7_30 − velocity_30_90, then
//                                    winsorised to the pipeline's OWN reported
//                                    clip bounds [-14.147, 9.575] (report 4.4)
//   revenue_volatility_60d        — rolling std-dev of Transient_Revenue over
//                                    the trailing 60 days as of inquiry_date
//   displacement_ema_7d           — 7-day-decay EMA of Total_Displacement_Cost
//                                    as of inquiry_date
//   night_variance_pct            — coefficient of variation of daily
//                                    Total_Occupancy_Pct across the RFP's own
//                                    stay-window nights (inferred from the name;
//                                    not documented anywhere in the provided
//                                    materials)
//
// LEFT AT 0 — genuinely no formula anywhere in the provided pipeline script,
// model report, or research PDF. Inventing one would misrepresent the model
// as more "model-driven" than it honestly is:
//   capacity_risk_score, revenue_intensity, tactical_compression_opportunity,
//   lead_time_deviation
//
// ── Live/future dates (no calendar coverage) ────────────────────────────────
// The real calendar only covers 2023-01-01..2025-12-31. Any RFP with an
// inquiry_date outside that range (i.e. every RFP submitted today, in 2026+)
// has no live transient data at all — this is the exact gap the original
// report flagged as "only misses transient data." Rather than silently
// returning 0 (which reads as "no risk/no demand" — a misleading signal) we
// fall back to a SEASONAL PROXY: the same calendar month+day in the most
// recent available year(s), averaged. This assumes transient demand
// seasonality repeats year over year, which is a reasonable operating
// assumption for a hotel's booking pattern but is NOT the same as live data.
// Every value computed this way is tagged `sourceIsProxy: true` in the
// returned object so callers/UI can disclose it if desired.

